.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_MKNOD 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_mknod
.Nd create a device node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_mknod "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_mknod
function creates a new device node named
.Fa name
in the directory
.Fa dvp .
The device identifier is specified by
.Fa dev .
If successful, the new vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The directory vnode.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the new vnode will be stored.
.It Fa cnp
The component name information for the new node.
.It Fa vap
The attributes (including mode and rdev) for the new node.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP"
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The vnode
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_create 9
